SUMMARY:Yoga in the Garden
DESCRIPTION:Join us at rare for Yoga in the Garden. \nLed by our instructor\, Chai\, this beginner-friendly\, all-levels class will be a gentle anchor to the land and our breath: \n\nSlow stretching to melt tension\n\n\nTwists to release old habits and emotional knots\n\n\nMeditation—the gift of slowing down\n\n\nBreathing practices that feel like sipping warm tea: steady\, comforting\, nurturing\n\nWe hope you’ll join us for this grounding\, heart-warming practice in nature and community. \nEvent Details \nCost: Free with a donation of food to the Cambridge Food Bank\nRegistration: Please register your attendance below. \nWhat to Bring: \n\nYour own yoga mat\nWater\nWeather-appropriate clothing\n\nMeeting Point:\nWe’ll gather in the parking lot at Springbank Garden\, 681 Blair Rd\, Cambridge\, at 9:20am and walk to the gardens together. \nInclement Weather Plan: \nIf the weather doesn’t cooperate\, we’ll relocate to the dry indoor space at Lamb’s Inn\, 1679 Blair Rd\, Cambridge. But we’ll be hoping for bright skies and the sounds of birdsong.
URL:https://ontarionature.org/event/yoga-in-the-garden/
LOCATION:Springbank Garden\, 681 Blair Road\, Cambridge\, Ontario\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Nature Network,Provincial Partners,Rare Charitable Research Reserve
ORGANIZER;CN="rare Charitable Research Reserve":MAILTO:rare@raresites.org
END:VEVENT
